---
import GuideLayout from '../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
const baseUrl = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith('/') ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : import.meta.env.BASE_URL + '/';
---

<GuideLayout 
  title="Hazards Guide"
  guideType="hazards"
>
  <h1>Hazards Guide</h1>
  
  <p>Hazards are environmental features that affect disc flight and scoring. Understanding how to play from different hazards is essential for lowering your scores and navigating challenging courses.</p>

  <h2>Hazard Types</h2>

  <h3>Rough</h3>
  <p>Rough terrain represents tall grass, brush, and difficult ground conditions.</p>
  
  <h4>Effects</h4>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Increased drag:</strong> Disc slows down more quickly when landing in rough</li>
    <li><strong>Reduced distance:</strong> Throws from rough travel shorter distances</li>
    <li><strong>Unpredictable bounces:</strong> Disc may bounce unpredictably on rough terrain</li>
    <li><strong>Difficulty:</strong> Moderate challenge for recovery shots</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Strategy</h4>
  <ul>
    <li>Use higher-speed discs to power through rough</li>
    <li>Aim for cleaner landing areas when possible</li>
    <li>Consider using OVERHAND stance for more predictable flight</li>
    <li>Play conservatively - focus on getting back in play rather than aggressive recovery</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Minimap Color</h4>
  <p><span style="color: #8B4513;">Brown</span> - Rough terrain appears as brown on the minimap</p>

  <h3>Sand</h3>
  <p>Sand hazards represent bunkers, beaches, and sandy areas that significantly affect disc flight.</p>
  
  <h4>Effects</h4>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Severe drag:</strong> Disc stops quickly when landing in sand</li>
    <li><strong>Burial risk:</strong> Disc may become partially buried</li>
    <li><strong>Power loss:</strong> Next throw has significantly reduced power</li>
    <li><strong>Difficulty:</strong> High challenge for recovery shots</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Strategy</h4>
  <ul>
    <li>Avoid sand at all costs on approach shots</li>
    <li>If in sand, play out sideways rather than trying to power through</li>
    <li>Use higher loft angles to escape sand traps</li>
    <li>Accept that recovery will cost strokes - play conservatively</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Minimap Color</h4>
  <p><span style="color: #F4A460;">Sandy Brown</span> - Sand appears as sandy brown on the minimap</p>

  <h3>Ice</h3>
  <p>Ice hazards represent frozen surfaces that reduce friction and cause unpredictable sliding.</p>
  
  <h4>Effects</h4>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Reduced friction:</strong> Disc slides much further on ice</li>
    <li><strong>Unpredictable direction:</strong> Slide direction can be hard to control</li>
    <li><strong>Speed maintenance:</strong> Disc maintains speed longer on ice</li>
    <li><strong>Difficulty:</strong> Variable - can help or hurt depending on situation</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Strategy</h4>
  <ul>
    <li>Account for extra slide distance when planning shots</li>
    <li>Use lower power to maintain control on icy surfaces</li>
    <li>Ice can be advantageous for long-distance slides if positioned well</li>
    <li>Avoid putting on ice - extremely difficult to control distance</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Minimap Color</h4>
  <p><span style="color: #ADD8E6;">Light Blue</span> - Ice appears as light blue on the minimap</p>

  <h3>Cactus</h3>
  <p>Cactus hazards represent desert vegetation that can damage discs and deflect throws.</p>
  
  <h4>Effects</h4>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Collision deflection:</strong> Disc bounces off cactus unpredictably</li>
    <li><strong>Durability damage:</strong> Repeated hits reduce disc durability</li>
    <li><strong>Blocked paths:</strong> Cactus can block direct lines to basket</li>
    <li><strong>Difficulty:</strong> High - requires precise shot shaping</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Strategy</h4>
  <ul>
    <li>Use PIERCE enchantment to ignore cactus collisions</li>
    <li>Shape shots around cactus rather than through them</li>
    <li>Hyzer and Anhyzer angles can navigate around cactus fields</li>
    <li>Consider OVERHAND for vertical clearance over cactus</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Minimap Color</h4>
  <p><span style="color: #228B22;">Forest Green</span> - Cactus appears as green on the minimap</p>

  <h3>Swamp</h3>
  <p>Swamp hazards represent wetlands, marshes, and waterlogged terrain.</p>
  
  <h4>Effects</h4>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Extreme drag:</strong> Disc stops almost immediately in swamp</li>
    <li><strong>Stuck risk:</strong> Disc may become stuck and unplayable</li>
    <li><strong>Penalty strokes:</strong> Swamp areas often carry stroke penalties</li>
    <li><strong>Difficulty:</strong> Very high - often requires relief</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Strategy</h4>
  <ul>
    <li>Avoid swamp entirely - plan routes around wetland areas</li>
    <li>If in swamp, take relief and penalty strokes rather than playing out</li>
    <li>Use elevated stances to keep disc above swamp vegetation</li>
    <li>Swamp is effectively a hazard zone - treat it like water</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Minimap Color</h4>
  <p><span style="color: #556B2F;">Dark Olive Green</span> - Swamp appears as dark green on the minimap</p>

  <h3>Lava</h3>
  <p>Lava hazards represent dangerous volcanic areas that destroy discs.</p>
  
  <h4>Effects</h4>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Disc destruction:</strong> Disc is destroyed if it lands in lava</li>
    <li><strong>Severe penalties:</strong> Lava carries maximum stroke penalties</li>
    <li><strong>Relief required:</strong> Must take relief from nearest safe point</li>
    <li><strong>Difficulty:</strong> Extreme - avoid at all costs</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Strategy</h4>
  <ul>
    <li>Never attempt shots over lava unless absolutely necessary</li>
    <li>Use extreme caution near lava hazards - play conservatively</li>
    <li>If forced to play near lava, aim well away from hazard edges</li>
    <li>Accept penalty strokes rather than risk disc loss</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Minimap Color</h4>
  <p><span style="color: #FF4500;">Orange Red</span> - Lava appears as orange-red on the minimap</p>

  <h3>Cliff</h3>
  <p>Cliff hazards represent elevation drops and steep terrain changes.</p>
  
  <h4>Effects</h4>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Elevation loss:</strong> Disc may fall down cliffs, adding distance</li>
    <li><strong>Unreachable lies:</strong> Disc may land in inaccessible positions</li>
    <li><strong>Line of sight:</strong> Cliffs can block direct shots to basket</li>
    <li><strong>Difficulty:</strong> Variable - depends on cliff height and accessibility</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Strategy</h4>
  <ul>
    <li>Use elevation to your advantage when possible</li>
    <li>Aim for cliff edges rather than going over - use backspin to stop near edge</li>
    <li>From below cliffs, use higher-loft shots to regain elevation</li>
    <li>Consider going around cliffs rather than trying to power over</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Minimap Color</h4>
  <p><span style="color: #808080;">Gray</span> - Cliffs appear as gray on the minimap</p>

  <h3>Water</h3>
  <p>Water hazards represent lakes, rivers, ponds, and other water features.</p>
  
  <h4>Effects</h4>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Hazard zone:</strong> Water is a designated hazard area</li>
    <li><strong>Penalty strokes:</strong> Landing in water incurs stroke penalties</li>
    <li><strong>Relief required:</strong> Must take relief from water hazard</li>
    <li><strong>Difficulty:</strong> High - requires course management</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Strategy</h4>
  <ul>
    <li>Avoid water at all costs on approach shots</li>
    <li>Play away from water rather than risking marginal shots</li>
    <li>Use layup shots to position safely away from water</li>
    <li>When forced to carry water, use plenty of clearance</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Minimap Color</h4>
  <p><span style="color: #0000FF;">Blue</span> - Water appears as blue on the minimap</p>

