  <h2>General Hazard Strategy</h2>

  <h3>Risk Management</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Assess the risk:</strong> Evaluate potential hazard vs. reward before each shot</li>
    <li><strong>Play the percentages:</strong> Choose high-percentage shots over low-percentage hero shots</li>
    <li><strong>Accept bogeys:</strong> Taking a conservative bogey is better than risking double bogey or worse</li>
    <li><strong>Know your limits:</strong> Don't attempt shots beyond your skill level</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Recovery Techniques</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Lateral movement:</strong> Often better to move sideways than directly toward target</li>
    <li><strong>Tempo control:</strong> Slower, controlled throws are often better from hazards</li>
    <li><strong>Stance selection:</strong> OVERHAND can provide more predictability from difficult lies</li>
    <li><strong>Angle management:</strong> Use release angles to shape shots around hazards</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Enchantment Help</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>PIERCE:</strong> Ignores vegetation collisions (cactus, rough)</li>
    <li><strong>STABILITY:</strong> Reduces fade for straighter recovery shots</li>
    <li><strong>RANGE:</strong> Extra distance can help escape deep hazards</li>
    <li><strong>DURABILITY:</strong> Reduces wear from hazard damage</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Biome-Specific Hazards</h2>
  <p>Different biomes have different hazard distributions:</p>

  <h3>Plains</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Primary hazards:</strong> Rough, occasional water</li>
    <li><strong>Difficulty:</strong> Low - most forgiving biome</li>
    <li><strong>Strategy:</strong> Aggressive play is viable</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Forest</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Primary hazards:</strong> Rough, cactus, cliffs</li>
    <li><strong>Difficulty:</strong> Moderate - requires shot shaping</li>
    <li><strong>Strategy:</strong> Precision over power, use gaps in vegetation</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Desert</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Primary hazards:</strong> Sand, cactus, lava</li>
    <li><strong>Difficulty:</strong> High - punishing hazards</li>
    <li><strong>Strategy:</strong> Avoid sand at all costs, play conservatively</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Mountain</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Primary hazards:</strong> Cliffs, rough, ice</li>
    <li><strong>Difficulty:</strong> High - elevation changes challenge</li>
    <li><strong>Strategy:</strong> Manage elevation carefully, account for slope</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Jungle</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Primary hazards:</strong> Rough, swamp, cactus</li>
    <li><strong>Difficulty:</strong> Very High - dense vegetation and wetlands</li>
    <li><strong>Strategy:</strong> Extreme precision required, accept penalties</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Ice</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Primary hazards:</strong> Ice, water, rough</li>
    <li><strong>Difficulty:</strong> Variable - ice can help or hurt</li>
    <li><strong>Strategy:</strong> Account for slide distance, use ice to advantage when possible</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Advanced Hazard Play</h2>

  <h3>Reading Hazard Layouts</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Use the minimap to identify hazard locations before throwing</li>
    <li>Plan multiple escape routes from each potential landing area</li>
    <li>Consider how wind will affect hazard interaction</li>
    <li>Identify "safe zones" to aim for rather than just avoiding hazards</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Shot Shaping for Hazards</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Hyzer:</strong> Useful for fighting headwinds near hazards</li>
    <li><strong>Anhyzer:</strong> Can curve around obstacle hazards</li>
    <li><strong>Flat:</strong> Most predictable for hazard avoidance</li>
    <li><strong>OVERHAND:</strong> Vertical clearance for height-based hazards</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Related Documentation</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href={`${baseUrl}guide/gameplay`}>Gameplay Mechanics</a></li>
